# tests/symlinks, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. It asserts on what a worker sees in a real /cas, so it IS a
# worker: std/bash as its base, the fixture bound as an arg, and no client or
# git worktree anywhere. It used to be a one-line cli.sh whose whole body was
# `$CAOS_CLI run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=check.sh` — a client test
# whose only job was to launch a worker test.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --tree:@=tree
